<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Stephen, King of England</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1092–1154</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Stephen of Blois, King Stephen</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Stephen was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> from 1135 to 1154, a grandson of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-the-conqueror">William the Conqueror</a> through his mother Adela and a son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stephen-count-of-blois">Stephen-Henry</a>, Count of Blois. He became count of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boulogne-sur-mer">Boulogne</a> by marrying its heiress Matilda and seized the English throne on the death of Henry I, against the claim of Empress Matilda. Their struggle, known as the Anarchy, ended when Stephen accepted her son Henry as his heir.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/stephen-king-of-england.jpg" alt="Stephen, King of England" width="210" height="522" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Henry of Huntingdon (Historia Anglorum) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Stepan_kral.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
